so if you aren't already aware apple  just came out and announced  three brand new products all running  apple silicon  but what does that mean for us  architects around the world in 2020  well today we're going to find out  what's going on guys my name is david  tomic and welcome back to the channel  today we're looking at the three brand  new products from apple  the macbook air the macbook pro and the  macbook mini  we're going to be looking at the apple  silicon architecture what this  m1 chip is and what it truly means for  us architects out there in 2020.  simply put the m1 chip is a combination  of multiple parts  previously used and combined through the  intel chip system  to make the computer powerful and run  now the m1 chip  combines some of the most powerful and  most important elements  in your computer today the m1 chip  combines  your cpu your gpu your graphics card  your data and power management and also  your security  it does a whole bunch of other features  as well but this is the primary elements  that truly contribute to how we operate  our systems from a day-to-day basis  some simple facts and figures for you  2.8 times  faster cpu five times faster gpu  and 5.9 times faster rendering  all of those sound fantastic if you're  comparing it  to your old device so if you're running  a macbook  pro right now you're gonna get two times  faster  cpu performance as an archicad user  myself personally speaking  i know that this will genuinely result  in a much better performance  when operating the system archicad runs  on predominantly  cpu requirements it only boots up the  graphics card  when you enter the 3d engine or when you  go into something  like twin motion and doing some  visualization i was in a meeting a  couple weeks ago discussing apple  silicon with the graphisoft team  and they personally said to me that they  have known about apple silicon for a  very long time now  and they are already ahead of the game  making sure that graphisoft is  compatible  once it launches which is now if you  just think about archicad and how  archicad started back in the day  it was originally approached by steve  jobs personally  to bring archicad to the apple software  so graphisoft and apple have a very  close  relationship and that will truly show as  we move forward  and graphisoft becomes even more  powerful and even more stable on  the new m1 chip breaking down the three  individual products  and potentially which one might be the  best for you as an architect in 2020  if you were to go out and purchase any  one of these  well it is a very tough decision to  break down  the cons first of all the macbook air  has  no fans and that is not a play on words  it is  actually genuinely a product without  any fans cooling the device  i know personally every time i run  archicad and then boot up photoshop  and open up i don't know twin motion and  then some illustrator and maybe some  chrome  all of a sudden my computer makes a hell  of a lot of noise  my computer behind me which is a custom  built rendering machine  still gets very loud and has to cool all  the time  so personally speaking i don't think the  macbook air  will be able to handle the power  requirements  of an architectural system and an  architectural software package  for the simple fact it won't be able to  cool it in time it'll get extremely hot  and potentially extremely dangerous now  i know the m1 chip is meant to be better  at performance  and thermal efficiency as well as power  management  however i genuinely don't see the  macbook air as a competitor  in the world of architecture in 2020.  stepping up to the macbook pro it does  have some fans  it has some mechanical cooling inside  which means it will be able to pump out  that hot air when it needs to  and also potentially remain very quiet  they are saying it is dead silent  nothing like the previous macbooks  which were annoyingly loud when you  needed to do anything  so this is potentially a truly useful  competitor  now when i say truly useful you have to  take this with a grain of salt  because what i mean is the simple fact  that any laptop you purchase  and if you haven't seen my top 20  laptops for 2020 for architects  i'll link it down below if you want to  take a look  is every laptop isn't going to be your  main daily driver  you really should be looking for a  product like a desktop or an imac  that you can sit at and run 24 7 because  you genuinely need  those high performance cores running all  the time  and not being split 50 50 between high  performance and  high efficiency cores like the m1 chip  is right now  so even though the macbook pro is  powerful enough to run  archicad and in my personal opinion more  than likely powerful enough  to run most projects in archicad to a  medium density scale  maybe five six units at a time  it probably shouldn't be your daily  driver it will however be a genuinely  good device  if you're out on the road going on a  holiday going on a plane trip somewhere  or just a simple work trip  if this is your device that you need to  carry along with you to quickly do some  work  it will be phenomenal however keep in  mind if you are an archicad  usbc dongles are extremely rare and  extremely limited  so you're going to have to go to the  cloud-based software k  options and last but not least the  macbook mini  now this is actually a fan favorite for  me it is a really nice device in a very  small compact package  however it hasn't been upgraded in a  very very long time  so even though it boasts some incredible  figures like 15 times  faster than the previous version of the  mac mini  it hasn't been updated whilst the  macbook pro and the macbook air  have been updated multiple multiple  times  so the macbook mini yes it is  significantly faster than the previous  generation  but it is still a very small compact  package  again i think it is on the same plane as  the macbook pro so if you're looking for  an alternative device  just to quickly run through some  drawings look at some information maybe  make some small changes  phenomenal device if you're looking for  a daily driver  i wouldn't recommend it in a nutshell  the m1 chip is an  extremely powerful and phenomenal step  forward  in innovation and architecture to have  all of your main components combined  into one  talking together as one brings us a step  closer to that  artificial intelligence that everybody's  worried about or dreaming about  if you're using archicad at the same  time it is a hundred percent  cpu based 90 of time unless you're in  the 3d window  so you're definitely going to see some  improved performance improved power  and a very visible noticeable change  from your previous computer  to your brand new m1 chip anyway that's  all for me today guys thank you so much  for watching i hope you enjoyed the  video  if you did make sure you smash that like  button down below to help this video  with the youtube algorithm  and if you want to see more of these  videos smash that subscribe button  leave a comment down below if you want  to see something specific  and as always i will see you next monday

